speechtext:
May I draw your attention, Mr. Speaker, to the fact that on page 6 of the bill, under the proposed section 32, it is stated as follows;
32. (1) Every one who conspires, combines, agrees or arranges with another person ... is guilty of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for two years.
As to the reference to a fine, while it is in the act at the moment, the amendment is to take fines out because the reference to fines is also covered in the Criminal Code and I submit it is a part of the bill.
